# The credentials file (docs/security.md, section 3): a secret, one line per
# SilverBullet user. Mount it read-only; the server re-reads it on change.
#
#   user   silverbullet-api-token   default-space   groups   bearer-hashes   [emails]
#
# default-space: the space used when a tool call names none, or -.
# groups: comma-separated, or -; they select @group entries of the access list.
# bearer-hashes: comma-separated hex SHA-256 digests of the client secrets,
#   one per client, or -. Make one with:  printf '%s' "$SECRET" | node src/main.ts --hash
# emails: optional; comma-separated e-mail addresses, or -. Behind Cloudflare
#   Access (docs/cloudflare-access.md) the address Access signed in selects the
#   line. An address belongs to one line only.
# The technical user of the scan is the line named by MCP_SCAN_USER (default
# `scan`); it needs no bearer and is never selected by an address.

writer-bot  sb_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx  notes  agents  3f1a…(64 hex digits)
reader-bot  sb_yyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyy  notes  agents  9b2c…,4e7d…
web-bot     sb_wwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwww  notes  agents  -            web-bot@example.org
scan        sb_zzzzzzzzzzzzzzzzzzzz  -      -       -
